Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At mas lalong nakakalungkot na tinitignan ng PNP ang praktikang ito

asr-001498
01:01:58.020 --> 01:01:59.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: bilang bagay na positibo.

asr-001499
01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:05.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At ito mismo ang nagpapakita kung gaano hinaharap ng administrasyon ng criticism.

asr-001500
01:02:05.580 --> 01:02:10.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, we will follow up with the rest of the pages.

asr-001501
01:02:11.160 --> 01:02:18.200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For now, Mr. Speaker, because the sponsor shared their concerns about school shooting

asr-001502
01:02:18.200 --> 01:02:27.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and ang role ng ECCD sa pagtaguyod na ang ating kabataan or ang mga bata

asr-001503
01:02:27.680 --> 01:02:28.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ay safe.

asr-001504
01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:38.020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and secure. Gusto rin po nating i-confront sila sa isang napakita natin

asr-001505
01:02:38.020 --> 01:02:42.940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: sa budget briefings noong ng Department of National Defense.

asr-001506
01:02:43.440 --> 01:02:46.360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I'm holding up a picture right now po, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001507
01:02:46.760 --> 01:02:50.660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Papakita ko po sa camera saglit bago po sa ating distinguished sponsor.

asr-001508
01:02:50.660 --> 01:02:58.660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ito po ay educational tour for 150 students of a child development center

asr-001509
01:02:59.180 --> 01:02:59.740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng Barangay.

asr-001510
01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:02.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Barangay North Poblasyon, Maramag, Bukidnon.

asr-001511
01:03:03.580 --> 01:03:10.340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At nakuha po natin itong picture na ito from the 89th Infantry Battalion Facebook page.

asr-001512
01:03:11.280 --> 01:03:18.100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Binapakita po nito ang picture na may mga bata in the tender ages of younger than six

asr-001513
01:03:18.100 --> 01:03:22.320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na may hawak po at pinapahawak po ng mga long firearms.

asr-001514
01:03:23.000 --> 01:03:28.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And this is a tour of a child development center, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001515
01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:32.520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang tanong po natin, katanggap-nanggap po ba ito?

asr-001516
01:03:33.220 --> 01:03:40.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May ensure po ba ng DILG na makakatuwang ang ECCD sa pagsigurado na walang ganitong educational tours

asr-001517
01:03:40.580 --> 01:03:43.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na gagawin ang child development centers?

asr-001518
01:03:43.340 --> 01:03:45.080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Moving forward, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001519
01:03:46.580 --> 01:03:48.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can you repeat that question again?

asr-001520
01:03:48.300 --> 01:03:53.940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yes, we will give the plenary page the copy of the photo.

asr-001521
01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:12.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay, so sometimes a picture says a thousand words.

asr-001522
01:04:13.480 --> 01:04:16.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay, so hindi ko pa talaga mayasagot.

asr-001523
01:04:16.640 --> 01:04:20.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But the advocacy is the safety of our kids.

asr-001524
01:04:20.880 --> 01:04:25.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So kasi kung tingnan niyo po talaga medyo hindi maganda.

asr-001525
01:04:25.600 --> 01:04:29.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero sa mga bata, baka pwedeng sinasabi rin na paano humawag.

asr-001526
01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:32.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Huwag nang kagamitan na safe.

asr-001527
01:04:32.740 --> 01:04:34.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But I totally agree with you.

asr-001528
01:04:35.320 --> 01:04:41.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have to call the attention of the agency regarding this picture.

asr-001529
01:04:42.700 --> 01:04:46.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So I think sa cabinet naman po, pwede pong pag-usapan po ito.

asr-001530
01:04:46.700 --> 01:04:49.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you for calling the attention of the DILG.

asr-001531
01:04:49.640 --> 01:04:51.120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001532
01:04:51.120 --> 01:04:59.120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang pinapakita ng scientific studies ay gun exposure at a young age increases instantaneously.

asr-001533
01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:04.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This is the result of the advances of accidental shootings and even perpetration of violence.

asr-001534
01:05:04.920 --> 01:05:10.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And nabanggit na rin naman po na mahalaga ang early childhood care and development.

asr-001535
01:05:11.040 --> 01:05:12.540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Gaya rin po nang sinabi ng sponsor.

asr-001536
01:05:13.240 --> 01:05:16.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So may commitment po ba na hindi na po ito mauulit.

asr-001537
01:05:16.740 --> 01:05:19.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Walang Child Development Center educational tour.

asr-001538
01:05:19.560 --> 01:05:28.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At makakatawang yung ECCD to ensure na ang pagpapatakbo ng mga CDC ay para po sa paglinang ng kabataan.

asr-001539
01:05:29.200 --> 01:05:29.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Hindi po sa mga...

asr-001540
01:05:29.780 --> 01:05:32.900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ganitong kinds of gun exposure, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001541
01:05:32.920 --> 01:05:34.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, we will commit to that.

asr-001542
01:05:34.320 --> 01:05:38.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We will investigate and we will commit na hindi na po ito mauulit.

asr-001543
01:05:38.980 --> 01:05:40.120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001544
01:05:40.200 --> 01:05:43.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Unfortunately, this just happened this year.

asr-001545
01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:46.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So sana po magkaroon ng kaagarang...

asr-001546
01:05:46.600 --> 01:05:48.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: If you can give me the date siguro, I can also...

asr-001547
01:05:48.920 --> 01:05:50.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yes po, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001548
01:05:50.640 --> 01:05:59.020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And just like in the past po, we express our deep concern in responding to the crisis of school shooting.

asr-001549
01:05:59.780 --> 01:06:08.380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And psychology experts and various scientific papers already proved that the approach to this topic must be centered on a child's mental health.

asr-001550
01:06:08.960 --> 01:06:17.900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And so it concerns us that with the most recent school shooting, not only is social media and the dark web blanketly blamed for it,

asr-001551
01:06:17.900 --> 01:06:25.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: although kailangan din investigahan yun, pero may mga iniisip na solusyon gaya po ng mga warrantless searches in the homes of gun owners.

asr-001552
01:06:26.000 --> 01:06:28.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So as a lawyer, I'd like to make it clear.

asr-001553
01:06:28.900 --> 01:06:29.740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: The violation of...

asr-001554
01:06:29.740 --> 01:06:32.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: The violation of a person's rights will not solve school violence.

asr-001555
01:06:33.200 --> 01:06:39.380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This representation can think of action steps it must first prioritize to ensure children do not commit school violence.

asr-001556
01:06:39.840 --> 01:06:46.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Gaya po ng better guidance of psychologists for mentors and parents to mitigate bullying and its effects on children.

asr-001557
01:06:46.900 --> 01:06:52.940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Digital literacy lessons for children so that they may taught at a young age to be critical of things they interact with online.

asr-001558
01:06:53.640 --> 01:06:57.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Stricter gun policies and monitoring for government employees with guns.

asr-001559
01:06:57.460 --> 01:06:59.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Given that the recent school shootings...

asr-001560
01:06:59.740 --> 01:07:08.640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Result of children na may access po sa guns ng parents and guardians na sila po ay members ng state forces or government employees.

asr-001561
01:07:09.240 --> 01:07:20.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, sa mga huli po natin sigurong tanong, pero ang una nating gustong i-raise ay na-raise po natin sa Dangerous Drugs Board.

asr-001562
01:07:20.040 --> 01:07:29.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This will be the final leg of questioning in relation po ito sa supposedly...

asr-001563
01:07:29.740 --> 01:07:46.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: DILG Memorandum Circular No. 2022-118, which makes anti-illegal drugs the mandatory peace and order and public safety or POPS focus area for every LGU.

asr-001564
01:07:46.680 --> 01:07:56.200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, nakita po natin na marami pong mga issues on peace and order, pero yung anti-illegal drugs yung center.

asr-001565
01:07:56.720 --> 01:07:59.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pwede po bang ma-enlighten kung ano pong...

asr-001566
01:07:59.740 --> 01:08:04.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yung assessment yung nagawa that singled out drugs as the mandatory category.

asr-001567
01:08:05.000 --> 01:08:16.760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And given po yung Dangerous Drugs Board's claimed shift to health and rights, yung circular po na ito na 2022 pa, under review po ba ito?

asr-001568
01:08:16.760 --> 01:08:20.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Meron po bang magiging amendment dito? Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001569
01:08:25.100 --> 01:08:27.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It's very hard to answer since it's a DDB.

asr-001570
01:08:29.740 --> 01:08:35.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And it's DILG also. DILG, Supervisionary Power over LGUs.

asr-001571
01:08:36.000 --> 01:08:46.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, well, ang ating pong kapulisan ay nagtatrabaho rin po talaga para po sugpuin ng illegal drugs.

asr-001572
01:08:47.280 --> 01:08:50.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And as I've mentioned, yung accomplishment report po nila.

asr-001573
01:08:50.960 --> 01:08:53.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, is it enough? I don't think so.

asr-001574
01:08:53.900 --> 01:08:54.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have to do more.

asr-001575
01:08:54.840 --> 01:08:58.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, we have to think of more ways.

asr-001576
01:08:58.620 --> 01:08:58.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Especially kung paano...

asr-001577
01:08:59.740 --> 01:09:02.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kung paano natin na protektahan ang ating pong mga kabataan.

asr-001578
01:09:03.320 --> 01:09:09.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, this regarding drugs is an issue between DDB and PDEA, ang head agency po dyan.

asr-001579
01:09:10.480 --> 01:09:17.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And bago po gumalaw ang kapulisan, dapat po ay deputize po sila ng PDEA.

asr-001580
01:09:17.840 --> 01:09:22.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Or else, I know you're a lawyer, technically, madidismiss po yung ating kaso.

asr-001581
01:09:23.580 --> 01:09:29.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We raised this question, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, dahil may sinabi nga pong shift.

asr-001582
01:09:29.740 --> 01:09:31.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: In health and rights.

asr-001583
01:09:31.620 --> 01:09:39.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero kung papansinin din po natin sa paggasta ng gobyerno, kung paano harapin yung anti-illegal drug operations,

asr-001584
01:09:39.880 --> 01:09:45.400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kalakhan po ng focus neto ay nasa criminalization aspect pa rin po.

asr-001585
01:09:45.400 --> 01:09:51.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ibig sabihin po, sa implementation ng POPs plans ng mga local government units natin,

asr-001586
01:09:52.360 --> 01:09:59.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: center pa rin po neto yung, well, intelligence, kung sino po ang mga drug users,

asr-001587
01:09:59.180 --> 01:10:02.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung sino po ang mga suppliers, etc.

asr-001588
01:10:03.060 --> 01:10:11.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At gusto natin makita kung dahil may claimed shift yung Dangerous Drugs Board na dapat pong may coordination with the ILG,

asr-001589
01:10:11.620 --> 01:10:16.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: paano po neto na-actualize away from a criminalization framework?

asr-001590
01:10:16.240 --> 01:10:19.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, actually, Madam, Mr. Speaker, it's a continuing effort.

asr-001591
01:10:20.220 --> 01:10:26.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, hindi po, porket ito na po yung ating palisya ngayon, ini-improve po po yan.

asr-001592
01:10:26.520 --> 01:10:29.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, depende po yan sa sitwasyon rin.

asr-001593
01:10:29.180 --> 01:10:33.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, continuing po siya, hindi po yan nakakalimutan ng DILG family.

asr-001594
01:10:34.340 --> 01:10:41.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Tumutulong po tayo dyan, tumutugon tayo dyan, lalo na meron po tayong mga officers din sa bawat LGUs.

asr-001595
01:10:41.600 --> 01:10:51.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, it will serve as a reminder na yung anong obligasyon ng buong sangay ng gobyerno, lalo na ng local government unit.

asr-001596
01:10:51.800 --> 01:10:53.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001597
01:10:53.440 --> 01:10:58.660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang update natin ng Dangerous Drugs Board ay this year daw po ay may i-release silang,

asr-001598
01:10:59.180 --> 01:11:07.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: enhanced Philippine, well, pads, na ito po yung pagharap sa anti-drug strategy nila,

asr-001599
01:11:08.000 --> 01:11:14.280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na implemented na raw po de facto, even though ay i-release pa lang po yung e-pads.

asr-001600
01:11:15.220 --> 01:11:23.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May update po ba, or pwede po bang malaman kung may nagbago na po ba sa LGU level plans, monitoring, and indicators?

asr-001601
01:11:23.960 --> 01:11:29.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: As of now, Mr. Speaker, wala pa pong update from DDB.

asr-001602
01:11:29.180 --> 01:11:31.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Papunta po sa DILG.

asr-001603
01:11:31.060 --> 01:11:41.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, ang punto po naman nito ay may mukhang disconnect sa paano po gusto ng Dangerous Drugs Board

asr-001604
01:11:41.680 --> 01:11:51.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na ituloy-tuloy ang anti-drug, anti-legal drug strategy, at paano po ito na i-implement sa ating LGUs.

asr-001605
01:11:51.800 --> 01:11:53.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, thank you for that question.

asr-001606
01:11:54.440 --> 01:11:58.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, somehow I know about DDB and PIDEA.

asr-001607
01:11:58.520 --> 01:12:02.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I handled the budget three years in the 19th Congress.

asr-001608
01:12:02.800 --> 01:12:05.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: DDB is policy, PIDEA is implementation.

asr-001609
01:12:06.300 --> 01:12:10.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But the problem is PIDEA, do they have sufficient men? No.

asr-001610
01:12:11.300 --> 01:12:13.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, minsan nga po, kailangan po deputize.

asr-001611
01:12:14.480 --> 01:12:17.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: May mga operational na ginagawa na po ang PIDEA.

asr-001612
01:12:17.660 --> 01:12:20.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Paano po padaliin ang pag-operate rin ng ating kapulisan?

asr-001613
01:12:21.160 --> 01:12:26.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Dahil very frustrating rin po sa ating kapulisan, lalo na pag may nahuli regarding drugs,

asr-001614
01:12:26.100 --> 01:12:28.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: because of certain technicalities,

asr-001615
01:12:28.520 --> 01:12:31.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: na hindi po nabigay ang papel ng PIDEA, etc.,

asr-001616
01:12:31.820 --> 01:12:33.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: nadidismiss po yung ating kaso.

asr-001617
01:12:34.260 --> 01:12:43.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, we recognize the problem, but the DILG is committed na mas maganda po sigurong pag-usapan pa lalo ng DDB,

asr-001618
01:12:43.860 --> 01:12:49.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: although wala po talagang directang mandato ang DILG doon,

asr-001619
01:12:49.080 --> 01:12:57.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: but since they are handling the police, so tama po kayo na dapat mas maganda yung pag-uusap at continuing on how to improve,

asr-001620
01:12:57.940 --> 01:13:01.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: lalo na ang ating operation regarding illegal drugs.

asr-001621
01:13:01.060 --> 01:13:12.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But one thing is for sure, hindi po natin kailangan na pumatay ng tao para po masugpo ang problema sa droga ng ating pong bansa.

asr-001622
01:13:12.380 --> 01:13:16.060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang huling tanong na lang po natin, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001623
01:13:16.060 --> 01:13:26.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kapansin-pansin sa mga POPs ng mga LGU, yung pinupondohang Barangay Intelligence Networks.

asr-001624
01:13:26.620 --> 01:13:26.820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ito po yung isa sa mga POPs ng mga LGU, yung pinupondohang Barangay Intelligence Networks.

asr-001625
01:13:26.820 --> 01:13:27.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ito po yung isa sa mga POPs ng mga LGU, yung pinupondohang Barangay Intelligence Networks.

asr-001626
01:13:27.920 --> 01:13:34.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ito po yung isa sa mga pinaka-heavily-funded items under anti-drugs POPs plans.

asr-001627
01:13:35.540 --> 01:13:45.020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At kasama po dito ang mga aktividad gaya ng recruiting informants, maintaining safe houses, identifying high-value and street-level individuals.

asr-001628
01:13:45.660 --> 01:13:54.760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ngunit wala pa tayong nakikitang specific issuance na nag-establish o nagbibigay ng regulasyon tungkol po sa pagkakaroon ng Barangay Intelligence Networks.

asr-001629
01:13:54.760 --> 01:13:57.880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Line item lang po siya sa mga LGU POPs plans.

asr-001630
01:13:57.920 --> 01:14:17.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So ang tanong po natin, Mr. Speaker, dahil napupondohan na ang Barangay Intelligence Networks for years now, at scale, meron po bang specific DILG or national issuance na may numero na maaari pong makahingi ang representasyon ng kopya na ito that authorizes and governs these Barangay Intelligence Networks?

asr-001631
01:14:17.920 --> 01:14:20.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At sa anong otoridad po ba ito?

asr-001632
01:14:20.840 --> 01:14:25.740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Now oversee yung informant recruitment, safe house use.

asr-001633
01:14:26.360 --> 01:14:26.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kapag...

asr-001634
01:14:26.920 --> 01:14:32.840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Nag-gather po ito, chinecheck kung effective yung paglabas po ng pondo, etc.

asr-001635
01:14:33.240 --> 01:14:35.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you for that question, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001636
01:14:35.620 --> 01:14:37.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's between the PNP and the LGU.

asr-001637
01:14:38.220 --> 01:14:40.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So on DILG po, has nothing to do about it.

asr-001638
01:14:41.120 --> 01:14:45.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So wala pong DILG issuance or national issuance na nag-govern po?

asr-001639
01:14:45.160 --> 01:14:49.960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I would like to remind, honorable ko, none, it's okay ha, none, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001640
01:14:50.460 --> 01:14:53.660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, just to wrap it up.

asr-001641
01:14:54.880 --> 01:14:56.760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Dahil napansin natin na...

asr-001642
01:14:56.920 --> 01:14:59.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Napakat laki ng pondo.

asr-001643
01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:04.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa Barangay Intelligence Networks, under POP's plans,

asr-001644
01:15:04.600 --> 01:15:08.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na kahit sinasabi natin nagbabago or nag-evolve continuously,

asr-001645
01:15:09.060 --> 01:15:13.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: pero ang DDB na mismo yung nagsabi na inaabandonan na ito dati

asr-001646
01:15:13.240 --> 01:15:17.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at ginagawa na yung bago, may malaking mismatch po talaga

asr-001647
01:15:17.920 --> 01:15:26.080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: doon sa paano nabibitbit sa baba ang mga ibang-ibang plano

asr-001648
01:15:26.080 --> 01:15:31.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na gustong i-implementa sa taas, na nakakadulot ng totoong harm,

asr-001649
01:15:32.420 --> 01:15:35.280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: lalo na sa mga biktima ng gera kontra droga,

asr-001650
01:15:35.360 --> 01:15:38.880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng kanilang mga pamilya na hanggang ngayon di pa rin po nakaka-recover

asr-001651
01:15:38.880 --> 01:15:40.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: totally, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001652
01:15:40.580 --> 01:15:45.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I have many other questions but I have run out of time, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001653
01:15:45.700 --> 01:15:51.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I will just simply conduct other questions via dialogue,

asr-001654
01:15:51.640 --> 01:15:55.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: but for now, there being no other questions,

asr-001655
01:15:55.600 --> 01:16:04.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: from the minority, I move to terminate the deliberation of the budget of the DILG

asr-001656
01:16:04.580 --> 01:16:07.260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and other attached agencies and corporations.

asr-001657
01:16:07.820 --> 01:16:08.860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So move, Mr. Chair.

asr-001658
01:16:09.160 --> 01:16:10.160
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: What does the House say?

asr-001659
01:16:10.700 --> 01:16:12.780
Floor Speaker: Mr. Speaker, on the part of the majority,

asr-001660
01:16:13.300 --> 01:16:16.860
Floor Speaker: we join the minority in their motion to terminate the budget

asr-001661
01:16:16.860 --> 01:16:22.460
Floor Speaker: of the Department of Interior and Local Government, including its attached agencies.

asr-001662
01:16:22.820 --> 01:16:23.240
Floor Speaker: So move.

asr-001663
01:16:23.240 --> 01:16:25.580
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: There is a joint motion.

asr-001664
01:16:25.600 --> 01:16:33.460
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: To terminate the interpellation on the proposed budget of the Department of the Interior and Local Government,

asr-001665
01:16:33.840 --> 01:16:35.620
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: including attached agencies.

asr-001666
01:16:36.100 --> 01:16:37.220
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: There is no objection.

asr-001667
01:16:38.240 --> 01:16:45.300
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Hearing none, the interpellation on the proposed budget of the Department of the Interior and Local Government,

asr-001668
01:16:45.920 --> 01:16:48.960
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: including attached agencies, is hereby terminated.

asr-001669
01:16:51.780 --> 01:16:52.860
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Majority Leader.

asr-001672
01:16:55.600 --> 01:16:57.220
Floor Speaker: Mr. Speaker, move to suspend session.

asr-001673
01:16:57.780 --> 01:16:59.180
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Session is suspended.

asr-001681
01:20:54.590 --> 01:20:59.480
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Mr. Speaker, I now move to consider the proposed budget of the Department of Tourism and its agencies.

asr-001682
01:20:59.480 --> 01:21:07.600
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: There is a motion to consider the budget of the Department of Tourism, including attached agencies and corporations.

asr-001683
01:21:07.600 --> 01:21:11.440
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Any objection? None. Motion is carried. Majority Leader.

asr-001684
01:21:11.440 --> 01:21:17.960
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Mr. Speaker, may we acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials from the Department of Tourism, namely:

asr-001685
01:21:17.960 --> 01:21:23.120
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Secretary [unclear], Undersecretary Stanley Ng,

asr-001686
01:21:23.120 --> 01:21:25.820
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Undersecretary Maria Dionne Rivera Guillermo,

asr-001688
01:21:25.840 --> 01:21:28.700
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Undersecretary Maria Victoria Jasmine.

asr-001689
01:21:29.120 --> 01:21:32.920
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Undersecretary Verna Esmeralda Buensuceso.

asr-001690
01:21:33.380 --> 01:21:35.440
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin.

asr-001691
01:21:36.040 --> 01:21:40.060
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Administrator-Attorney Joanne Padilla of Intramuros Administration.

asr-001692
01:21:40.640 --> 01:21:45.020
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Executive Director Cecile Lorenzana, National Parks Development Committee.

asr-001693
01:21:45.600 --> 01:21:49.980
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Executive Director Marco Angelo Acheta, Philippine Commission on Sports.

asr-001694
01:21:49.980 --> 01:21:55.460
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Dr. Mark Lapid, Chief Operating Officer, Tourism Infrastructure and Enterprise Zone,

asr-001695
01:21:55.580 --> 01:22:01.680
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Authority, Chief Operating Officer, Maria Margarita Montemayor Nograles Tourism Promotions Board,

asr-001696
01:22:02.180 --> 01:22:06.940
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Chief Operating Officer, Patrick Joel Cinco, Duty Free Philippines Corporation,

asr-001697
01:22:07.540 --> 01:22:11.660
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: General Manager Roberto Zozobrado, Philippine Retirement Authority,

asr-001698
01:22:12.180 --> 01:22:17.080
Rep. Ronald V. Singson: Executive Director Leonila Fabul of Nayong Pilipino Foundation.

asr-001699
01:22:17.080 --> 01:22:23.540
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: In behalf of Speaker Boji D. and Majority Leader Sandro Marcos,

asr-001700
01:22:24.500 --> 01:22:25.080
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: we welcome the...

asr-001701
01:22:25.580 --> 01:22:29.980
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: D.O.T. heads and officials to the House of Representatives.

asr-001702
01:22:30.840 --> 01:22:31.980
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Majority Leader.

asr-001703
01:22:33.980 --> 01:22:41.260
Rep. De Carlo L. Uy: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Marie Bernadette G. Escudero,

asr-001704
01:22:41.920 --> 01:22:44.920
Rep. De Carlo L. Uy: Vice Chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations,

asr-001705
01:22:45.840 --> 01:22:49.440
Rep. De Carlo L. Uy: to answer questions on the proposed budget of the Department of Tourism.

asr-001706
01:22:50.480 --> 01:22:54.180
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The gentlelady from the 1st District, Sor Sogon,

asr-001707
01:22:54.340 --> 01:22:55.480
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Vice Chair on...

asr-001708
01:22:55.580 --> 01:22:58.080
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The Honorable Maria Bernadette Escudero.

asr-001709
01:22:58.580 --> 01:23:00.000
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Ma'am, you may start.

asr-001710
01:23:01.440 --> 01:23:02.820
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Salamat, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001711
01:23:03.900 --> 01:23:06.020
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues,

asr-001712
01:23:06.700 --> 01:23:10.640
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: I rise today to sponsor the proposed budget of the Department of Tourism

asr-001713
01:23:10.640 --> 01:23:14.440
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and its attached agencies for fiscal year 2027.

asr-001714
01:23:15.860 --> 01:23:18.160
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Tourism is an investment that multiplies.

asr-001715
01:23:18.840 --> 01:23:21.320
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: The government may provide the first peso,

asr-001716
01:23:21.320 --> 01:23:25.320
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: but tourism allows that peso to move through our economy.

asr-001717
01:23:25.580 --> 01:23:33.780
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Umiikot mula sa airport, papunta sa hotel, restaurants, tour guides, transport operators,

asr-001718
01:23:33.780 --> 01:23:37.780
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: magsasaka, souvenir shops at maliliit na negosyo.

asr-001719
01:23:37.780 --> 01:23:44.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And along the way, that one peso becomes income, jobs, and livelihoods for millions of Filipinos.

asr-001720
01:23:44.580 --> 01:23:48.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: We already see this happening across our economy.

asr-001721
01:23:48.580 --> 01:23:54.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: In 2025, tourism directly generated 2.27 trillion in economic value,

asr-001722
01:23:54.580 --> 01:23:59.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: equivalent to 8.1% of our GDP.

asr-001723
01:23:59.580 --> 01:24:04.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Domestic travelers spent 3.26 trillion,

asr-001724
01:24:04.580 --> 01:24:11.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: while international visitors brought approximately 698 billion into our economy.

asr-001725
01:24:11.580 --> 01:24:15.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Tourism also supported 7.7 million jobs,

asr-001726
01:24:15.580 --> 01:24:20.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: or 15.7% of total employment in the Philippines.

asr-001727
01:24:20.580 --> 01:24:23.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, behind those numbers are people,

asr-001728
01:24:23.580 --> 01:24:24.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: the hotel employee

asr-001729
01:24:24.580 --> 01:24:27.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: who depends on a steady flow of guests,

asr-001730
01:24:27.580 --> 01:24:30.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: the tour guide waiting for the next group of visitors,

asr-001731
01:24:30.580 --> 01:24:34.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: the restaurant owner, the driver, the souvenir maker,

asr-001732
01:24:34.580 --> 01:24:36.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and the small business owner.

asr-001733
01:24:36.580 --> 01:24:38.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: They tell us something very important.

asr-001734
01:24:38.580 --> 01:24:40.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: When we invest in tourism,

asr-001735
01:24:40.580 --> 01:24:43.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: the benefits do not stay within the tourism sector.

asr-001736
01:24:43.580 --> 01:24:46.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: They spread across our economy.

asr-001737
01:24:46.580 --> 01:24:48.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, dear colleagues,

asr-001738
01:24:48.580 --> 01:24:51.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: at the 2025 World Travel Awards,

asr-001739
01:24:51.580 --> 01:24:53.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: the Philippines was named Asia's leading beach destination.

asr-001740
01:24:53.580 --> 01:24:57.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Asia's leading dive destination.

asr-001741
01:24:57.580 --> 01:25:00.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And Asia's leading island destination.

asr-001742
01:25:00.580 --> 01:25:05.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: It was our seventh consecutive year as Asia's leading dive destination

asr-001743
01:25:05.580 --> 01:25:10.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and our eighth recognition as Asia's leading beach destination.

asr-001744
01:25:10.580 --> 01:25:13.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Our appeal also goes beyond leisure travel.

asr-001745
01:25:13.580 --> 01:25:18.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: The Philippines was recognized as Asia's best retirement destination in 2025.

asr-001746
01:25:18.580 --> 01:25:22.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And this year was named world's number one retirement destination

asr-001747
01:25:22.580 --> 01:25:27.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: for 2026 in the Retirement Abroad Index.

asr-001748
01:25:27.580 --> 01:25:32.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So the challenge is not whether Philippine tourism has value.

asr-001749
01:25:32.580 --> 01:25:35.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: The challenge is unlocking its full scale.

asr-001750
01:25:35.580 --> 01:25:38.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And promotion is central to that effort.

asr-001751
01:25:38.580 --> 01:25:41.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Building on the Love the Philippines campaign,

asr-001752
01:25:41.580 --> 01:25:45.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: the department has introduced Discover More to Love,

asr-001753
01:25:45.580 --> 01:25:48.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: reinforcing our existing brand while encouraging travelers

asr-001754
01:25:48.580 --> 01:25:51.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to discover more of our destinations,

asr-001755
01:25:51.580 --> 01:25:54.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: experiences, culture, and people.

asr-001756
01:25:54.580 --> 01:25:57.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, the objective is conversion.

asr-001757
01:25:57.580 --> 01:25:59.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: From seeing the Philippines,

asr-001758
01:25:59.580 --> 01:26:02.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to wanting to visit the Philippines,

asr-001759
01:26:02.580 --> 01:26:05.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to actually booking a trip to the Philippines.

asr-001760
01:26:05.580 --> 01:26:10.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: This objective requires the resources to reach the markets we are competing for.

asr-001761
01:26:10.580 --> 01:26:12.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: For fiscal year 2027,

asr-001762
01:26:12.580 --> 01:26:17.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: the National Expenditure Program proposes approximately 4 billion

asr-001763
01:26:17.580 --> 01:26:20.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: of the Department of Tourism and its attached agencies,

asr-001764
01:26:20.580 --> 01:26:27.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: around 196 million lower than the fiscal year 2026 General Appropriations Act.

asr-001765
01:26:27.580 --> 01:26:30.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: This includes 1 billion for the Global Branding Campaign

asr-001766
01:26:30.580 --> 01:26:34.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: together with approximately 1.37 billion budget

asr-001767
01:26:34.580 --> 01:26:37.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: of the Tourism Promotions Board.

asr-001768
01:26:37.580 --> 01:26:41.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Our resources for tourism promotions remain far smaller

asr-001769
01:26:41.580 --> 01:26:45.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: than those of several of our major ASEAN competitors.

asr-001770
01:26:45.580 --> 01:26:48.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Available comparative figures put Philippine tourism marketing spending

asr-001771
01:26:48.580 --> 01:26:51.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: at around 86 million U.S. dollars,

asr-001772
01:26:51.580 --> 01:26:56.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: compared with approximately 499 million U.S. dollars for Thailand,

asr-001773
01:26:56.580 --> 01:26:59.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: 418 million for Singapore,

asr-001774
01:26:59.580 --> 01:27:02.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and 331 million U.S. dollars for Malaysia.

asr-001775
01:27:02.580 --> 01:27:07.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, we are competing for the same international travelers.

asr-001776
01:27:07.580 --> 01:27:10.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Every destination is trying to capture their attention,

asr-001777
01:27:10.580 --> 01:27:14.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: convince them to book, and persuade them to stay and spend.

asr-001778
01:27:14.580 --> 01:27:17.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: If we want a greater share of that market,

asr-001779
01:27:17.580 --> 01:27:20.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: we must be prepared to compete for it.

asr-001780
01:27:20.580 --> 01:27:23.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Promotion, however, is only one part of the effort.

asr-001781
01:27:23.580 --> 01:27:27.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Tourism works best when government works together.

asr-001782
01:27:27.580 --> 01:27:32.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: We want visitors to arrive easily, move around efficiently,

asr-001783
01:27:32.580 --> 01:27:36.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: discover more destinations, and leave wanting to come back again.

asr-001784
01:27:36.580 --> 01:27:39.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: That requires a whole-of-government effort,

asr-001785
01:27:39.580 --> 01:27:43.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: because visitors do not experience our agencies separately.

asr-001786
01:27:43.580 --> 01:27:46.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: They simply experience the Philippines.

asr-001787
01:27:46.580 --> 01:27:48.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Given limited fiscal space,

asr-001788
01:27:48.580 --> 01:27:52.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: additional resources must be targeted where they can make the greatest difference.

asr-001789
01:27:52.580 --> 01:27:55.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Scuba diving is one clear example.

asr-001790
01:27:55.580 --> 01:28:00.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Our dive tourism industry is estimated at 1.3 billion U.S. dollars.

asr-001791
01:28:00.580 --> 01:28:05.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: We have 29 dive destination clusters, 956 identified dive sites,

asr-001792
01:28:05.580 --> 01:28:09.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and we have been recognized as Asia's leading dive destination

asr-001793
01:28:09.580 --> 01:28:11.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: for seven consecutive years.

asr-001794
01:28:11.580 --> 01:28:15.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: An additional 82.49 million for the Philippine Commission on Sports Scuba Diving

asr-001795
01:28:15.580 --> 01:28:20.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: would support the development and promotion of dive tourism,

asr-001796
01:28:20.580 --> 01:28:25.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: improve data monitoring, and strengthen emergency response capabilities.

asr-001797
01:28:25.580 --> 01:28:30.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: This is the kind of targeted investment that can reach beyond the tourism activity itself

asr-001798
01:28:30.580 --> 01:28:34.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to resorts, dive professionals, transport operators,

asr-001799
01:28:34.580 --> 01:28:38.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: restaurants, and businesses in our coastal communities.

asr-001800
01:28:38.580 --> 01:28:42.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: One tourism product can support an entire local economy.

asr-001801
01:28:42.580 --> 01:28:45.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: The same principle applies to our cultural heritage.

asr-001802
01:28:45.580 --> 01:28:48.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Intramuros is one such opportunity.

asr-001803
01:28:48.580 --> 01:28:52.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Next year, the Intramuros Administration intends to advance its effort again

asr-001804
01:28:52.580 --> 01:28:55.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: toward UNESCO World Heritage Recognition

asr-001805
01:28:55.580 --> 01:28:59.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and is seeking additional funding support for the work needed

asr-001806
01:28:59.580 --> 01:29:02.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to strengthen the walled city's conservation, management,

asr-001807
01:29:02.580 --> 01:29:05.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and readiness for the UNESCO process.

asr-001808
01:29:05.580 --> 01:29:09.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Tourism development is not always about building something new.

asr-001809
01:29:09.580 --> 01:29:12.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Sometimes it is about protecting what we already have

asr-001810
01:29:12.580 --> 01:29:15.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and allowing the world to experience it.

asr-001811
01:29:15.580 --> 01:29:21.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: The industry already contributes 2.27 trillion directly to our economy.

asr-001812
01:29:21.580 --> 01:29:25.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: It already supports 7.7 million Filipino jobs.

asr-001813
01:29:25.580 --> 01:29:30.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Our tourism products are already receiving international recognition.

asr-001814
01:29:30.580 --> 01:29:33.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: The case before us is not whether tourism matters.

asr-001815
01:29:33.580 --> 01:29:36.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: The numbers have already answered that.

asr-001816
01:29:36.580 --> 01:29:40.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: The question is how much more value we can create from the tourism economy

asr-001817
01:29:40.580 --> 01:29:44.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and how much of that value can reach our people.

asr-001818
01:29:44.580 --> 01:29:47.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And that is why I respectfully urge this Chamber

asr-001819
01:29:47.580 --> 01:29:51.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to support the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget

asr-001820
01:29:51.580 --> 01:29:54.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: of the Department of Tourism and its attached agencies

asr-001821
01:29:54.580 --> 01:29:59.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and to seriously consider the necessary augmentation for its programs.

asr-001822
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:02.900
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Let us give Philippine tourism the resources to compete.

asr-001823
01:30:03.500 --> 01:30:06.800
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Let us give more travelers a reason to love the Philippines.

asr-001824
01:30:07.440 --> 01:30:11.040
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And when they come, more reasons to discover, more to love.

asr-001825
01:30:11.680 --> 01:30:14.360
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker, esteemed colleagues.

asr-001826
01:30:17.220 --> 01:30:19.740
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Thank you, Vice Chair Escudero, Majority Leader.

asr-001827
01:30:19.740 --> 01:30:33.200
Rep. De Carlo L. Uy: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Iris Marie de Mesa Montes of Partylist 4K to interpolate the sponsor on the proposed budget.

asr-001828
01:30:33.980 --> 01:30:40.320
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The gentlelady from 4K, Partylist Representative Iris Marie de Mesa Montes is recognized. Please proceed.

asr-001829
01:30:40.760 --> 01:30:41.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-001830
01:30:42.360 --> 01:30:44.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mr. Chair, distinguished colleague,

asr-001831
01:30:45.200 --> 01:30:49.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: While the Philippines boasts of world-class destinations,

asr-001832
01:30:49.740 --> 01:30:56.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: tourism arrivals remain far below potential compared to our ASEAN neighbors.

asr-001833
01:30:57.320 --> 01:31:05.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: May we ask the department exactly what are the specific challenges that prevent us from maximizing arrivals

asr-001834
01:31:05.480 --> 01:31:12.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and what concrete strategies are funded in the 2027 budget to overcome these bottlenecks?

asr-001835
01:31:14.120 --> 01:31:16.640
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Salamat po sa tanong, distinguished colleague.

asr-001836
01:31:17.580 --> 01:31:19.640
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Before I begin po, let me...

asr-001837
01:31:19.740 --> 01:31:22.460
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: share the numbers, no?

asr-001838
01:31:22.680 --> 01:31:24.960
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: From 2023 up to 2025,

asr-001839
01:31:25.860 --> 01:31:29.960
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: nag-increase po ng 18.4% ang tourist arrivals natin.

asr-001840
01:31:29.960 --> 01:31:33.920
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: From 2023, 5.477 million.

asr-001841
01:31:34.600 --> 01:31:39.360
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Ngayong 2025 ay 6.484 million.

asr-001842
01:31:39.840 --> 01:31:42.960
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So kahit pa pano po, tumaas ng 18.4%.

asr-001843
01:31:43.580 --> 01:31:49.040
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And it is also notable po, no?

asr-001844
01:31:49.740 --> 01:31:50.520
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Distinguished colleague,

asr-001845
01:31:51.960 --> 01:31:53.720
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: na from 2023 also,

asr-001846
01:31:54.380 --> 01:31:57.580
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: number 6 po tayo in ranking sa ASEAN.

asr-001847
01:31:58.340 --> 01:32:01.820
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: At noong 2024, bumaba ng konti, naging number 7.

asr-001848
01:32:01.820 --> 01:32:06.300
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Pero noong 2025, umangat uli tayo sa number 6,

asr-001849
01:32:07.060 --> 01:32:09.440
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: na may 6.4 million tourist arrivals.

asr-001850
01:32:09.840 --> 01:32:13.120
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Number 1 po is Thailand, number 2, Malaysia, number 3, Vietnam,

asr-001851
01:32:13.780 --> 01:32:16.040
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: number 4, Singapore, number 5, Indonesia.

asr-001852
01:32:17.280 --> 01:32:18.460
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: But it is also notable,

asr-001853
01:32:19.100 --> 01:32:19.540
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: um,

asr-001854
01:32:19.740 --> 01:32:20.680
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: distinguished colleague,

asr-001855
01:32:21.260 --> 01:32:23.120
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: na pagdating po sa marketing budget,

asr-001856
01:32:24.160 --> 01:32:28.040
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: medyo maliit po talaga yung nabigay sa ating departamento.

asr-001857
01:32:28.040 --> 01:32:33.900
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Ang budget po natin for 2025 ay 86.68 million dollars.

asr-001858
01:32:34.440 --> 01:32:39.920
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: As compared po to 499 million for Thailand,

asr-001859
01:32:40.520 --> 01:32:42.320
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: 418 million for Singapore,

asr-001860
01:32:42.620 --> 01:32:46.060
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and 331 million for Malaysia.

asr-001861
01:32:46.880 --> 01:32:49.500
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, um, to be blunt po, talagang,

asr-001862
01:32:49.740 --> 01:32:51.740
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: medyo nahuhuli po tayo sa ASEAN,

asr-001863
01:32:51.840 --> 01:32:58.440
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: kasi tayo din po yung isa sa may pinakamababang budget po for the department.

asr-001864
01:32:59.100 --> 01:33:02.640
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And, um, it is also notable po na kahit mas mababa,

asr-001865
01:33:03.000 --> 01:33:04.940
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: mas mababa pa yung budget natin,

asr-001866
01:33:05.780 --> 01:33:08.740
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: kinumpute po natin yung arrivals per million, no?

asr-001867
01:33:09.080 --> 01:33:10.760
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Base po dun sa gastos.

asr-001868
01:33:11.240 --> 01:33:13.920
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And, um, based on arrivals per million,

asr-001869
01:33:13.920 --> 01:33:18.920
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: makikita po natin na we have 74,758 arrivals

asr-001870
01:33:19.740 --> 01:33:23.080
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: tourist arrivals per 1 million na ginastos.

asr-001871
01:33:23.080 --> 01:33:25.040
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: As compared po to Thailand,

asr-001872
01:33:25.680 --> 01:33:33.260
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: which has 66,053 arrivals per 1 million na ginastos.

asr-001873
01:33:33.780 --> 01:33:37.400
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, kaya po ganun kalaki din yung naging tourist arrivals nila

asr-001874
01:33:37.400 --> 01:33:41.280
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: dahil napakalaki din po yung in-invest nila sa promotions.

asr-001875
01:33:41.500 --> 01:33:45.140
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Gagaya nga ng sinabi ko kanina sa sponsorship speech ko,

asr-001876
01:33:45.260 --> 01:33:47.600
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: isa lang po yung pinag-aagawan natin ng mga turista.

asr-001877
01:33:48.160 --> 01:33:49.700
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, kung sino talaga,

asr-001878
01:33:49.700 --> 01:33:52.400
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: yung mas may malaking promotion budget,

asr-001879
01:33:52.780 --> 01:33:56.080
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: talagang mas nae-engganyo yung mga turista na pumunta sa kanila.

asr-001880
01:33:56.740 --> 01:33:58.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Chair.

asr-001881
01:33:59.600 --> 01:34:03.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tungkol naman po dun sa abolition ng travel tax.

asr-001882
01:34:04.200 --> 01:34:09.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Naipasa na po ng Kongreso yung panukalang batas to abolish the travel tax.

asr-001883
01:34:10.180 --> 01:34:15.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, mawawalan po ng funding stream yung TIEZA projects, ano?

asr-001884
01:34:16.080 --> 01:34:19.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Malaki po ba ang epekto nito sa ating tourism?

asr-001885
01:34:19.700 --> 01:34:32.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At kung sakali po, paano po mautugunan ng ahensya kung sakaling mawalan na ng funding stream yung TIEZA

asr-001886
01:34:32.360 --> 01:34:35.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: galing dito sa travel tax abolition?

asr-001887
01:34:37.620 --> 01:34:42.020
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

asr-001888
01:34:42.760 --> 01:34:46.740
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: for year 2026, existing pa po yung travel tax collections.

asr-001889
01:34:46.740 --> 01:34:49.080
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Dito po sa lower house, napasa na po.

asr-001890
01:34:49.700 --> 01:34:55.500
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: On third reading, pero as we speak po, pending pa po ang consideration in the Senate.

asr-001891
01:34:55.820 --> 01:35:01.880
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, as of now, mapupondahan po yung mga projects natin under TIEZA.

asr-001892
01:35:04.080 --> 01:35:10.160
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: To give an idea po, for 2025, 4.4 billion po yung pondo for TIEZA.

asr-001893
01:35:10.820 --> 01:35:18.520
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: But, if abolished po yung House Bill po natin na 8464, as approved on third reading,

asr-001894
01:35:18.520 --> 01:35:24.680
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: sinabi naman po na kung hindi na po makakakolekta ng travel tax, which will fund TIEZA.

asr-001895
01:35:24.920 --> 01:35:30.340
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Actually, hindi lang po TIEZA, kasama po doon ang CHED and NCCA, pupondohan po ito through the GAA.

asr-001896
01:35:31.260 --> 01:35:33.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay. Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-001897
01:35:33.780 --> 01:35:37.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yung susunod naman po tungkol sa Tourism Road Infrastructure Program.

asr-001898
01:35:38.280 --> 01:35:41.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito po, alam naman natin, ito yung Convergence Program with DPWH,

asr-001899
01:35:41.960 --> 01:35:47.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: which is actually cornerstone for access roads and tourism infrastructure.

asr-001900
01:35:47.640 --> 01:35:48.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Meron po ba tayong...

asr-001901
01:35:48.500 --> 01:35:53.060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang alokasyon sa 2027 para dito sa mga proyektong ito?

asr-001902
01:35:54.260 --> 01:35:59.040
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, to be blunt po, zero po.

asr-001903
01:35:59.240 --> 01:36:03.480
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Zero po yung allocation natin for the TRIP program.

asr-001904
01:36:04.780 --> 01:36:13.200
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Base po sa records, no, simula po 2025, hindi na po nagkaroon ng pondo for new TRIP programs.

asr-001905
01:36:13.200 --> 01:36:15.040
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Lahat po yung continuing.

asr-001906
01:36:15.760 --> 01:36:17.460
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Ganon din po noong 2026.

asr-001907
01:36:17.720 --> 01:36:18.280
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Continuing.

asr-001908
01:36:18.500 --> 01:36:19.940
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Programs na lang po for the TRIP.

asr-001909
01:36:20.060 --> 01:36:22.420
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Wala din pong new programs.

asr-001910
01:36:22.660 --> 01:36:29.360
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And for 2027, both new and continuing po ay zero po ang pondo.

asr-001911
01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:37.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mr. Speaker, again, ano po kaya ang magiging epekto na naman nito sa ating tourism industry?

asr-001912
01:36:37.940 --> 01:36:41.080
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Sa totoo lang po, napakalaki po yung magiging epekto nito.

asr-001913
01:36:41.080 --> 01:36:47.700
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Dahil ang pinorposed po na budget ng DOT ay 28 projects po amounting to 6 billion.

asr-001914
01:36:47.700 --> 01:36:49.780
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: For year 2027.

asr-001915
01:36:50.060 --> 01:36:53.540
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, hindi po talaga alam ng department kung saan kukunin tong pondong ito.

asr-001916
01:36:55.480 --> 01:36:59.020
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Sinubmit po nila ito sa DPWH and also sa DBM.

asr-001917
01:36:59.220 --> 01:37:05.340
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: But unfortunately, dahil nga po kulang ng fiscal space, hindi po na provide yung budget na nire-request.

asr-001918
01:37:06.060 --> 01:37:08.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001919
01:37:08.620 --> 01:37:17.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano naman po ang portion sa 2027 budget natin na allocated for digital tourism, marketing, and online platforms?

asr-001920
01:37:17.020 --> 01:37:23.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Given that global travelers now rely on digital channels for destination choices.

asr-001921
01:37:29.780 --> 01:37:38.280
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Yung bago pong campaign ng DOT, yung Discover More to Love, it is a reinforcement initiative under the Love the Philippines campaign.

asr-001922
01:37:38.960 --> 01:37:45.120
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: It is actually an online platform where the government partners with the private sector such as airlines, hotels, and tour operators

asr-001923
01:37:45.120 --> 01:37:46.840
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to offer travel deals.

asr-001924
01:37:47.020 --> 01:37:50.280
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and discounts, and encourage more people to travel around the country.

asr-001925
01:37:50.800 --> 01:37:58.960
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, in just a few months po, the website has already sold 203,000 airline seats and 800 room nights.

asr-001926
01:38:00.440 --> 01:38:05.420
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, it actually helps bring in travelers, generate bookings, and support our tourism businesses.

asr-001927
01:38:05.900 --> 01:38:11.620
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Especially at this time na tumaas po yung fuel cost, kaya medyo mas bumaba talaga yung turismo sa atin.

asr-001928
01:38:11.820 --> 01:38:16.400
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: But beyond this po, the Discover More to Love, expound ko na lang din.

asr-001929
01:38:17.020 --> 01:38:24.240
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Since we're at it, the DOT has also tapped BINI and SB19, creating dedicated microsites for them

asr-001930
01:38:24.240 --> 01:38:29.520
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: where fans can explore Philippine destinations through the artists they follow and admire.

asr-001931
01:38:31.160 --> 01:38:33.340
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Malaki po at maganda po yung response.

asr-001932
01:38:33.480 --> 01:38:42.620
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: In just two weeks after the microsites were launched, the DOT website where these microsites are hosted recorded 44,000 new users.

asr-001933
01:38:42.800 --> 01:38:47.000
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, hopefully, magta-translate din to more visitors.

asr-001934
01:38:47.020 --> 01:38:50.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Chair, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-001935
01:38:50.680 --> 01:38:55.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Huling tanong na lamang po, tungkol naman po ito sa tourism workforce training.

asr-001936
01:38:56.220 --> 01:39:03.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano naman po ang mga programa? What programs are funded in the 2027 budget to upscale tourism workers?

asr-001937
01:39:04.460 --> 01:39:08.300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yung guides, hospitality, staff, and local entrepreneurs.

asr-001938
01:39:08.540 --> 01:39:11.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, service quality matches global standards.

asr-001939
01:39:17.020 --> 01:39:37.500
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, as mentioned kanina in my sponsorship speech, meron po tayong 7.7 million employed Filipinos na tinutulungan ng Department of Tourism.

asr-001940
01:39:41.340 --> 01:39:44.620
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Under accommodation and food and beverage,

asr-001941
01:39:45.080 --> 01:39:46.500
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: ang total employment po natin ay...

asr-001942
01:39:47.020 --> 01:39:49.020
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: 2,907,000.

asr-001943
01:39:56.220 --> 01:40:05.300
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Isa po sa mga programa sa workforce natin ay ang Tourism Industry Training Program.

asr-001944
01:40:05.300 --> 01:40:16.520
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, it benefits 64,000 direct training beneficiaries that focuses on training courses, digitalization and technology, and certification and ladderization programs.

asr-001945
01:40:17.560 --> 01:40:18.980
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Yun po.

asr-001946
01:40:20.920 --> 01:40:28.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yun lamang po, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, maraming salamat po to the Department of Tourism.

asr-001947
01:40:29.200 --> 01:40:30.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you po.

asr-001948
01:40:30.400 --> 01:40:31.980
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Thank you very much, Majority Leader.

asr-001949
01:40:33.780 --> 01:40:41.220
Rep. De Carlo L. Uy: Mr. Speaker, next to interpelate the sponsor, I move to recognize Representative Sergio Dago'ok of Partylist APEC.

asr-001950
01:40:41.300 --> 01:40:46.560
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The gentleman from APEC Partylist, Representative Sergio Dago'ok is recognized.

asr-001951
01:40:47.020 --> 01:40:51.220
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Thank you, Majority Leader.

asr-001952
01:40:52.740 --> 01:40:58.160
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Magandang gabi po sa ating sponsor at sa pamilya ng Department of Tourism.

asr-001953
01:40:59.020 --> 01:41:08.740
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Would the Distinguished Sponsor yield to some clarificatory questions regarding the budget of the Department of Tourism?

asr-001954
01:41:08.800 --> 01:41:09.860
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Of course, po. Gladly.

asr-001955
01:41:11.420 --> 01:41:14.140
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Unang-una, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-001956
01:41:17.020 --> 01:41:25.660
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: May nakalaan tayo na 1 billion para sa branding campaign. Tama po ba?

asr-001957
01:41:26.420 --> 01:41:27.120
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Tama po yan.

asr-001958
01:41:28.320 --> 01:41:40.740
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So, ang budget ba na ito, mayroong mga measurable performance indicators?

asr-001959
01:41:42.640 --> 01:41:43.740
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Tama po yan.

asr-001960
01:41:45.040 --> 01:41:46.740
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kandi, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-001961
01:41:47.020 --> 01:42:00.860
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Distinguished Sponsor, give some specific measurable performance sa branding.

asr-001962
01:42:01.960 --> 01:42:12.300
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ano po yung mga key performance indicators na tumalab at nagiging efektibo yung branding strategy natin?

asr-001963
01:42:17.020 --> 01:42:24.640
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, as mentioned kanina po, yung ginawa po na Love the Philippines campaign, part po ito ng ating branding campaign,

asr-001964
01:42:25.380 --> 01:42:36.200
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: in just 2 months, the website has already sold 203,000 airline seats, 800 room nights,

asr-001965
01:42:37.200 --> 01:42:43.820
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and yung microsites po na nilaunch, recorded 44,000 new users,

asr-001966
01:42:43.820 --> 01:42:46.900
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and also, as mentioned also a while ago po,

asr-001967
01:42:47.020 --> 01:42:52.180
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, nag-produce din po ng 7.7 million jobs,

asr-001968
01:42:52.740 --> 01:42:57.220
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and may contribution din po sa ating GDP na 8.1%.

asr-001969
01:42:57.220 --> 01:43:00.480
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: So, I think po, Mr. Speaker, more than anything,

asr-001970
01:43:01.060 --> 01:43:08.300
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: dun po talaga natin mamimesure na ang contribution po ng Department of Tourism sa ekonomiya ay napakalaki talaga.

asr-001971
01:43:11.100 --> 01:43:15.380
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ang mga numero po ba na yan ay mas mataas?

asr-001972
01:43:17.020 --> 01:43:21.040
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Compared doon sa dating branding strategy natin?

asr-001977
01:44:14.550 --> 01:44:20.160
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, actually tumaas po yung yield ng campaign from 33 percent

asr-001978
01:44:20.160 --> 01:44:23.520
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: To 35 percent. Tumaas po ng 2 percent.

asr-001979
01:44:23.520 --> 01:44:33.760
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ano po yung percentage na yan? What specific performance indicator?

